[{:db/id "q-80146/selection/33a64b97da32a2a93027cd07004cacfac59dded1609476b25fe1d4459702f1af" :answer/id #uuid "23cf9da3-434e-5f9e-8a10-2436474de581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80146/selection/4486a87f82694a1526b4c056f0e01a751ace24d43150d4760fde9392249d5351" :answer/id #uuid "09eeb433-2a85-57aa-870a-52b38a61e105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80146/selection/dd8024e0699af6dc5779446a08950a7c825dafbf7465fd438a835e43f1a9d4b9" :answer/id #uuid "af228ee3-52d7-5bcf-ba5e-338b9ec211d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80146/selection/56eefad87e977e71b7b8f7bd0b146b0e23830aa063efa828586fff6e9cd01cc4" :answer/id #uuid "dce0b15f-d564-5ab9-9ebe-2c29e722c6f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80146/selection/3aa280d4c75b99c35e6132545de4bf1b477f587c7d4c8f824aeafaa204f9fda1" :answer/id #uuid "77eafdff-caca-5a16-a3e6-8a38b4472323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80146/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c272c3c0-986c-546a-99f7-8bf122ae15db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80146/selection/33a64b97da32a2a93027cd07004cacfac59dded1609476b25fe1d4459702f1af" :answer-field/choices ["q-80146/selection/33a64b97da32a2a93027cd07004cacfac59dded1609476b25fe1d4459702f1af" "q-80146/selection/4486a87f82694a1526b4c056f0e01a751ace24d43150d4760fde9392249d5351" "q-80146/selection/dd8024e0699af6dc5779446a08950a7c825dafbf7465fd438a835e43f1a9d4b9" "q-80146/selection/56eefad87e977e71b7b8f7bd0b146b0e23830aa063efa828586fff6e9cd01cc4" "q-80146/selection/3aa280d4c75b99c35e6132545de4bf1b477f587c7d4c8f824aeafaa204f9fda1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80146" :question/id #uuid "6cc7e6a3-0859-5323-8766-9f81ba79e12a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80146" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =3+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =12 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{60}^{∘})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-80146/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80146"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107568/selection/c36d8e96571cdbf597a19e132beacc2024b3a0b861ce9c1df29a3e6ad67ff94e" :answer/id #uuid "4000dabe-ee68-5f33-9510-5953ab147453" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107568/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "1695464c-3348-5af8-9745-e2e2abfebae1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107568/selection/a50d63d40594c6206b5da036765609c56a8b6f95e39ed3333ee0e0bf0b53e02e" :answer/id #uuid "dec6057e-03a6-589e-b6a4-eb5c1638a7f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2\\sqrt{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107568/selection/b1c905da1b4268aa23055645fd285620d6f81a98278a19acab248d281a65e810" :answer/id #uuid "f4ecd30a-f9c8-549c-81e5-308edc034b2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107568/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "21b05d78-1943-5ba1-84ea-e36cd0c391a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107568/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd8e72e-803d-5f4d-b6de-aca6e8783284" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107568/selection/c36d8e96571cdbf597a19e132beacc2024b3a0b861ce9c1df29a3e6ad67ff94e" :answer-field/choices ["q-107568/selection/c36d8e96571cdbf597a19e132beacc2024b3a0b861ce9c1df29a3e6ad67ff94e" "q-107568/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" "q-107568/selection/a50d63d40594c6206b5da036765609c56a8b6f95e39ed3333ee0e0bf0b53e02e" "q-107568/selection/b1c905da1b4268aa23055645fd285620d6f81a98278a19acab248d281a65e810" "q-107568/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107568" :question/id #uuid "ca1309a0-4449-5728-8b2d-e41d4c8dcb20" :question/math-academy-id "q-107568" :question/problem "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107568/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107568"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274595/field-1/d5d6348fb64beebdf3e447915877b40d7f7dd26c7ba4be1f3a84b9f6919d4d52" :answer/id #uuid "020dfe61-d022-5bb0-ab50-a9c632306a03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{53}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274595/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d87fb09-2a0c-529b-953a-1b72612e9822" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274595/field-1/d5d6348fb64beebdf3e447915877b40d7f7dd26c7ba4be1f3a84b9f6919d4d52" :answer-field/choices ["q-274595/field-1/d5d6348fb64beebdf3e447915877b40d7f7dd26c7ba4be1f3a84b9f6919d4d52"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274595/field-2/deddd6ccfff814f2bfb1adc56b59602b7a823d75f738581a900082eff59c6d88" :answer/id #uuid "798ab3fa-9a8e-5ebd-a4fd-0eb92900724b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.292" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274595/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "639419d8-f500-536b-8414-741be1b2f05e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274595/field-2/deddd6ccfff814f2bfb1adc56b59602b7a823d75f738581a900082eff59c6d88" :answer-field/choices ["q-274595/field-2/deddd6ccfff814f2bfb1adc56b59602b7a823d75f738581a900082eff59c6d88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274595" :question/id #uuid "e39ad95c-4cfe-5a21-89b5-bc6e60c91a5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-274595" :question/problem "Express $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Use the **exact value** for $R,$ and round $ϕ$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈1.292\\,\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ) & ={7}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ)) & =49+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =53 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{53}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)≈\\sqrt{53}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.292)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274595/field-1" "q-274595/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274595"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328001/field-1/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "d5955b6f-a71f-5a90-afcc-3a04689f218f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328001/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "82429dc1-0204-5edc-bb88-bac397d5cb58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328001/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "40f3302c-0baf-5f9e-b08a-22cea308cc45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328001/field-1/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer-field/choices ["q-328001/field-1/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" "q-328001/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328001/field-2/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "b3cdace3-65b5-59bf-a4ff-38644ae2cc2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328001/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cff5dcd-a27a-50e1-9523-b7f4dd619547" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328001/field-2/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer-field/choices ["q-328001/field-2/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328001" :question/id #uuid "085c668f-2506-5811-898e-24d7fef4cd51" :question/math-academy-id "q-328001" :question/problem "Express $-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ in the form $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,{90}^{∘}).$\n\n$-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$\n {{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘})$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =9+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =18 \\\\ R & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{45}^{∘})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328001/field-1" "q-328001/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328001"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328007/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "f93f09fc-39ab-5750-a7ef-fedf2de9173a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328007/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1dd7a562-4547-5253-bf53-e2a1ef676797" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328007/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-328007/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328007" :question/id #uuid "d6d5e026-b5b1-568e-9a62-9b03769713f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-328007" :question/problem "Given that the expression $-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+ϕ)$ with $0<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0,$ what is the value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for cosine gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ ϕ & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-328007/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328007"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
